      { "step": "Auditions", "text": "Rappers from across the country perform original material. The strongest make it into the top 15 or 16 who compete on the show." },
      { "step": "Squads", "text": "From season 2 onward, contestants are split into squads led by squad bosses. In season 3 Badshah made the first assignments, and squad bosses could use a 'mic drop' to pull a contestant into their own squad." },
      { "step": "Weekly challenges", "text": "Each week brings a theme, from original songs to collaborations and head-to-head battles such as the Battleground round." },
      { "step": "Danger zone and voting", "text": "The weakest performers land in the danger zone. Squad bosses can save a contestant, and public votes also shape who is eliminated." },
      { "step": "Grand finale", "text": "The last contestants standing perform in a two-night finale for the title, prize money and prizes from the season's sponsors." },
      { "step": "OG Hustler", "text": "From season 3 the show also names an OG Hustler, a separate award with its own cash prize for the contestant who best represents the spirit of the hustle." }
    ],
